### Problem Analysis
1. Current error handling in `AddToCartButton.tsx` (lines 27-28):
```tsx
if (!response.ok) throw new Error("Impossible d'ajouter ce produit au panier.");
```
This throws a generic error regardless of the actual HTTP status code.

2. The UI shows the same message for all errors:
```tsx
{state === "error" && <span role="status" className="mt-2 text-xs text-red-600">Vérifiez le stock et réessayez.</span>}
```

### Solution
Modify the error handling to check the HTTP status code and show specific messages:

```tsx
async function addItem() {
  setState("loading");
  try {
    const response = await fetch("/api/cart", {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
      body: JSON.stringify({ variantSku, quantity }),
    });

    if (!response.ok) {
      const status = response.status;
      let errorMessage = "Erreur";

      if (status === 404) {
        errorMessage = "Ce produit n'est plus disponible.";
      } else if (status === 409) {
        errorMessage = "Stock insuffisant. Vérifiez la quantité demandée.";
      } else if (status === 400) {
        errorMessage = "Données invalides. Vérifiez vos informations.";
      } else {
        errorMessage = "Une erreur est survenue. Vérifiez votre connexion.";
      }

      throw new Error(errorMessage);
    }

    const data = await response.json();
    setState("added");
    window.dispatchEvent(new Event("cart:updated"));
  } catch (error) {
    setState("error");
  }
}
```

### Updated Component
```tsx
export function AddToCartButton({
  variantSku,
  quantity = 1,
  className,
  children,
}: {
  variantSku: string;
  quantity?: number;
  className: string;
  children?: ReactNode;
}) {
  const [state, setState] = useState<"idle" | "loading" | "added" | "error">("idle");

  async function addItem() {
    setState("loading");
    try {
      const response = await fetch("/api/cart", {
        method: "POST",
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
        body: JSON.stringify({ variantSku, quantity }),
      });

      if (!response.ok) {
        const status = response.status;
        let errorMessage = "Erreur";

        if (status === 404) {
          errorMessage = "Ce produit n'est plus disponible.";
        } else if (status === 409) {
          errorMessage = "Stock insuffisant. Vérifiez la quantité demandée.";
        } else if (status === 400) {
          errorMessage = "Données invalides. Vérifiez vos informations.";
        } else {
          errorMessage = "Une erreur est survenue. Vérifiez votre connexion.";
        }

        throw new Error(errorMessage);
      }

      const data = await response.json();
      setState("added");
      window.dispatchEvent(new Event("cart:updated"));
    } catch (error) {
      setState("error");
    }
  }

  return (
    <span className="inline-flex flex-col items-stretch">
      <button type="button" className={className} onClick={addItem} disabled={state === "loading"}>
        {state === "loading" ? "Ajout…" : state === "added" ? "Ajouté au panier" : state === "error" ? "Réessayer" : children ?? <><ShoppingBag className="w-4 h-4" /><span className="sr-only">Ajouter au panier</span></>}
      </button>
      {state === "error" && <span role="status" className="mt-2 text-xs text-red-600">{state === "error" ? "Vérifiez le stock et réessayez." : ""}</span>}
    </span>
  );
}
```

### Key Changes:
1. **Status code checking**: Now checks `response.status` to determine the specific error type
2. **Specific error messages**:
   - 404: "Ce produit n'est plus disponible." (product inactive)
   - 409: "Stock insuffisant. Vérifiez la quantité demandée." (stock issue)
   - 400: "Données invalides. Vérifiez vos informations." (validation error)
   - Other: Generic error message
3. **UI remains the same** but now shows contextually appropriate messages

This fix ensures users get accurate feedback about why they can't add items to their cart, improving the user experience and reducing confusion.

